<title>NETHERLANDS: PAYS-BAS PROPERTY 1996 NET PROFIT SURGES.</title>
<headline>PAYS-BAS PROPERTY 1996 NET PROFIT SURGES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>Direct investment income (net profit)  17.3  vs  10.9</p>
<p>    Ditto per share (guilders		   0.46 vs   0.30</p>
<p>    Net rental income			    37.4  vs  32.9</p>
<p>    Financial charges			    14.8  vs  16.2</p>
<p>    Operating costs				 5.3  vs   5.8</p>
<p>    Positive property revaluation	     1.6  vs   0.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Since December 1996, Pays-Bas Property Fund is</p>
<p>majority-owned by VastNed Offices/Industrial which has</p>
<p>announced it would launch a bid for the remaining shares.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
